.\" tcp.7 - Substrate TCP
.TH TCP 7 "2026-09-23" "Substrate" "Substrate Programmer's Manual"
.SH NAME
tcp \- TCP protocol
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B #include <netinet/in.h>
.B #include <netinet/tcp.h>
.PP
.IB tcp_socket " = socket(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, 0);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Substrate's TCP follows RFC 793 as amended by RFC 1122, with RFC 5681
congestion control and RFC 5961 protection against blind resets.
A connection has a 32 KiB receive buffer; there is no send buffer, so a
.BR write (2)
returns once its data has been queued for transmission within the peer's
window.
.PP
Data that arrives out of order is held for reassembly.
The advertised window follows receiver silly-window avoidance, and the
sender applies the Nagle algorithm and sender silly-window avoidance.
While the peer advertises a zero window, one-octet probes are sent for as
long as the peer keeps answering them.
.PP
Data left unacknowledged is retransmitted with exponential backoff.
The connection is aborted with
.B ETIMEDOUT
when the retransmission budget of the oldest segment is exhausted, or
when no unacknowledged data has been acknowledged for the
.I user timeout
(300 seconds unless set with
.BR TCP_USER_TIMEOUT ).
A connection with nothing outstanding is never timed out.
.SS Socket options
Options at level
.B IPPROTO_TCP
are set with
.BR setsockopt (2)
and read with
.BR getsockopt (2).
.TP
.B TCP_USER_TIMEOUT
An
.I unsigned int
of milliseconds (RFC 5482): how long transmitted data may remain
unacknowledged before the connection is aborted with
.BR ETIMEDOUT .
Zero, the default, selects the system value of 300 seconds.
An explicit value also bounds zero-window probing, which the default
does not.
Connections accepted from a listening socket inherit its value.
.PP
Other
.B IPPROTO_TCP
options are accepted without effect.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I optlen
is smaller than an
.IR int ,
or
.B TCP_USER_TIMEOUT
was given a negative value.
.TP
.B ENOPROTOOPT
.B TCP_USER_TIMEOUT
was used on a socket that is not a TCP socket.
.TP
.B ETIMEDOUT
Reported by
.BR read (2),
.BR write (2)
or
.B SO_ERROR
when the connection was aborted by the retransmission budget or the user
timeout.
.SH EXAMPLE
Abort a connection after 30 seconds without acknowledgement:
.PP
.EX
unsigned int ms = 30000;
if (setsockopt(fd, IPPROTO_TCP, TCP_USER_TIMEOUT, &ms, sizeof ms) < 0)
    perror("setsockopt");
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR socket (2),
.BR setsockopt (2),
.BR getsockopt (2),
.BR shutdown (2)
